WEBVTT

00:02.512 --> 00:05.413
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.816 --> 00:09.149
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.253 --> 00:12.519
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.858 --> 00:15.656
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.861 --> 00:18.990
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.298 --> 00:22.324
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.435 --> 00:24.096
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.203 --> 00:25.728
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.839 --> 00:30.572
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:36.251 --> 00:39.449
Oh, Joe, thank you so much for
inviting us to your barbecue.

00:39.555 --> 00:41.079
Well, it's my pleasure, Lois.

00:41.190 --> 00:43.055
Hey, can one of you other men
come over here

00:43.158 --> 00:44.888
and comment on the meat
while I'm cooking it?

00:44.995 --> 00:46.519
Yeah, I got it.

00:47.297 --> 00:51.564
Yeah. Those are looking good.
Yeah, that's what I'm talking about.

00:51.702 --> 00:54.796
Yeah, don't flip them too often now.
You don't want to lose the juices.

00:54.906 --> 00:59.344
Yeah. Yeah, coming along nicely.
Yeah, those are cooking just fine.

00:59.444 --> 01:02.140
Scoop that one up and put it back down
in the exact same spot.

01:02.247 --> 01:04.045
All right, they're done! Time to eat!

01:04.150 --> 01:06.846
Oh, boy! I'm so hungry I could eat a horse.

01:08.421 --> 01:10.913
I... uh... I misspoke.

01:13.527 --> 01:16.690
Wow, Bonnie! You really took off
the baby weight quickly.

01:16.797 --> 01:18.163
Oh, thanks, Lois.

01:18.266 --> 01:20.996
Hey, do you mind rubbing
some of that sunblock on my back?

01:21.102 --> 01:25.039
Of course, Bonnie.
Oh, but I don't want to get any on my shirt.

01:27.710 --> 01:30.236
Mmm... That feels good.

01:32.649 --> 01:37.644
- Um, you're going a little low there, Lois.
- Okay. I'm sorry.

01:39.657 --> 01:40.715
Giggity!

01:43.128 --> 01:45.824
Aw, Joe, Susie's such a cute baby.

01:45.931 --> 01:47.455
Hey, whatever happened to your son,
Kevin?

01:47.566 --> 01:49.558
- He died in Iraq.
- Sad.

01:49.903 --> 01:52.303
"I won't let you walk out of here
without that dress. "

01:52.405 --> 01:54.396
"I don't know. Will I ever wear it?"
"Yes, you will.

01:54.507 --> 01:56.703
"You've got that thing for the opening
of the library next week.

01:56.811 --> 01:58.335
"It's perfect for that. "

01:58.446 --> 02:01.142
"Hey, everybody. "
"Oh! Look. It's black Barbie.

02:01.248 --> 02:04.650
"Why are you all alone?"
"Oh, they discontinued my boyfriend.

02:04.753 --> 02:07.950
"Mom says I'm the one
whose hair it's okay to cut. "

02:09.525 --> 02:11.459
Hey! I was playing with that!

02:11.561 --> 02:14.724
Hey, come back here!
All right. You asked for it.

02:16.967 --> 02:18.264
Holy crap!

02:19.036 --> 02:21.504
All right. Let's try that one again.

02:29.582 --> 02:30.810
Oh, my God! Stewie!

02:31.017 --> 02:33.884
Your kid got beat up by a baby girl!

02:33.986 --> 02:35.887
Oh, man! This is more painful to watch

02:35.989 --> 02:38.651
<i>than when Family Ties
does a Tina Yothers episode.</i>

02:39.026 --> 02:40.823
<i>Jennifer, what happened in school today?</i>

02:40.927 --> 02:42.054
<i>I got my period!</i>

02:42.163 --> 02:44.791
And I will see the Keaton family next week.

02:49.438 --> 02:52.601
Okay now, sweetie.
This isn't gonna hurt at all.

02:53.776 --> 02:55.802
Those lying bastards
at Johnson & Johnson!

02:56.179 --> 02:59.842
- We'll put, "No more tears" on the label.
- But it does make you cry.

02:59.983 --> 03:01.008
I know.

03:08.493 --> 03:10.552
Lois, you should just let
those wounds get infected.

03:10.662 --> 03:12.391
It'll teach him a lesson about being tough.

03:12.497 --> 03:15.399
Peter, he's just a baby.
You got to let this go.

03:15.501 --> 03:17.901
My baby boy got beat up by a girl.

03:18.104 --> 03:20.437
What was weird was that she was crying,

03:20.541 --> 03:24.272
but the way she was standing over me
made it look like I was crying,

03:24.378 --> 03:25.572
which was weird.

03:25.679 --> 03:28.444
Peter, what exactly are you worried
is gonna happen because of this?

03:28.550 --> 03:31.075
- World War V.
- Peter, we've been over this.

03:31.186 --> 03:33.951
There has to be a World War llI
and IV first.

03:34.056 --> 03:36.217
Oh, no. Oh, no.
That's the beauty of World War V, Lois.

03:36.325 --> 03:38.555
It's so intense it skips over the other two.

03:38.661 --> 03:41.495
- Peter, it doesn't work...
- I have spoken!

03:46.237 --> 03:49.206
There's Connie D'Amico.
Chris, don't walk next to me.

03:49.907 --> 03:53.241
Hi, Connie. Uh, so, I heard you talking
in the hall the other day

03:53.345 --> 03:55.279
<i>about how much you liked
High School Musical 2</i>

03:55.380 --> 03:59.647
- so I burned you the soundtrack.
- Okay. Prepare for itemized insults.

03:59.752 --> 04:02.983
A. Don't ever listen to me talk.
You don't deserve my words.

04:03.089 --> 04:06.389
B. When I said I enjoyed it,
I was speaking ironically.

04:06.494 --> 04:09.486
<i>And C.
You actually like High School Musical?</i>

04:09.597 --> 04:11.896
What are you? Eight? No, that's impossible

04:12.000 --> 04:15.436
because I've seen that big hairy mudflap
ass of yours in the locker room.

04:15.537 --> 04:17.664
- Questions?
- Hey, Meg. Take that!

04:20.309 --> 04:21.401
That was awesome!

04:21.511 --> 04:23.240
The joke's kind of on us
because we're smelling it.

04:23.346 --> 04:25.076
Yeah!
Awesome!

04:25.182 --> 04:27.241
Way to go!
Sweet!

04:27.718 --> 04:30.846
Scott is such an idiot.
I'm totally breaking up with him.

04:30.954 --> 04:33.150
I'm gonna switch to
one of the other popular guys.

04:33.258 --> 04:36.250
But, Connie, you've gone out with,
like, every popular boy in this school.

04:36.361 --> 04:39.456
Yeah, you're right.
God, they all suck so much.

04:39.565 --> 04:43.524
I need a new challenge. What if...
Wait. Now, bear with me on this.

04:43.636 --> 04:47.198
What if I date a loser
and make him over into a popular guy?

04:47.307 --> 04:49.605
Wow! Great idea! I'm glad I hung in there!

04:49.709 --> 04:52.372
Now, who are the biggest losers
in this school?

04:52.580 --> 04:55.606
- Well, there's Smiley McGee.
- Hello.

04:55.716 --> 04:57.981
Nah. I hear he's a bed-wetter.

04:58.420 --> 05:02.413
And Chris Griffin.
- Oh, my God! I can smell him from here.

05:02.624 --> 05:04.490
- He's perfect.
- God, you're right.

05:04.594 --> 05:06.585
He smells like Fred Flintstone's ass.

05:06.696 --> 05:09.426
Hey! No one's asking you to smell it!

05:13.003 --> 05:16.063
All right, Stewie. Your dad's gonna
help you learn how to be a man.

05:16.173 --> 05:19.940
Real men have a couple of beers and then
project their inadequacies on their kids.

05:20.045 --> 05:21.069
- Okay.
- What's that?

05:21.179 --> 05:23.512
- You think you're better than me?
- What? No. I didn't say that.

05:23.616 --> 05:26.585
So I guess you think you would have
been some kind of big shot by my age, huh?

05:26.686 --> 05:28.551
Done things differently?
Gotten that promotion?

05:28.654 --> 05:31.385
- I don't even know what you do.
- Well, let me tell you something!

05:31.491 --> 05:34.654
You're nothing,
and you're never gonna be nothing!

05:34.861 --> 05:37.456
Now, let's sit here and watch Spike TV.

05:37.565 --> 05:40.534
<i>Spike TV, full of stuff men like.</i>

05:47.576 --> 05:49.204
<i>Yeah, that stuff.</i>

05:55.253 --> 05:58.654
Wow, my favorite.
PB and J with the crusts cut off.

05:58.756 --> 06:00.690
- What did you get?
- Your crusts.

06:00.791 --> 06:02.089
- That's it?
- No.

06:02.194 --> 06:05.755
I also got an orange peel
and a picture of Mom eating a turkey leg.

06:08.835 --> 06:11.827
Oh, my God! Connie's coming over
to talk to me! Sit up straight!

06:11.938 --> 06:15.534
- Hey, Meg, nice posture. Get lost.
- Thank you.

06:16.176 --> 06:20.169
Chris Griffin, you are undoubtedly
the most unpopular boy in school.

06:20.281 --> 06:23.251
I am?
What about Smiley McGee over there?

06:24.052 --> 06:25.314
Hello.

06:25.520 --> 06:27.853
You and I are going on a date
Saturday night.

06:27.957 --> 06:30.517
- Um... Okay.
- I'll see you then.

06:31.294 --> 06:32.955
Why would she go out with me?

06:33.062 --> 06:36.499
She must be more drunk than Santa Claus
when he got that DUl.

06:36.867 --> 06:41.464
No, no. It wasn't my fault.
Some guy in a Plymouth totally cut me off.

06:41.572 --> 06:44.837
- Sir, they don't make Plymouths anymore.
- Are you Jewish?

06:44.942 --> 06:46.967
Sir, I'm gonna need you to
step out of the sleigh.

06:51.684 --> 06:54.017
All right, Stewie.
We're gonna get you nice and pumped up.

06:54.120 --> 06:58.318
Now, you see that barbell over there?
Go ahead and try and lift that.

07:01.062 --> 07:03.690
Uh-oh, spadoodios.

07:03.798 --> 07:05.425
I notice your kid is having some trouble.

07:05.533 --> 07:08.765
- You're telling me.
- Oh, your kid just needs a little help.

07:08.904 --> 07:10.895
I got something that'll get him going.

07:13.042 --> 07:14.441
Well, if there's anyone I can trust,

07:14.544 --> 07:17.104
it's a stranger at the gym
holding a dirty needle.

07:17.213 --> 07:20.047
- Here, Stewie. Try this.
- What the hell are you...

07:20.150 --> 07:25.611
Oh, my! Suddenly I'm full
of energy! All right, fat man! Let's do this!

07:47.382 --> 07:51.648
- Wow, Stewie! You look like a new man.
- Well, will you look at me?

07:52.087 --> 07:54.851
I have the power!

07:54.957 --> 07:56.015
<i>He-Man</i>

08:02.699 --> 08:05.965
<i>We now return to
Lady and the Tramp and Michael Vick.</i>

08:17.777 --> 08:19.267
Hello, family.

08:21.680 --> 08:23.341
Does anyone need the remote?

08:23.449 --> 08:25.884
Oh, my God!
What the hell happened to Stewie?

08:25.986 --> 08:27.476
Yeah, looks good. Doesn't he?

08:27.587 --> 08:30.488
Let's see that little dyke, Susie Swanson,
beat him up now.

08:30.591 --> 08:32.024
Wait a minute.
How do you know she's gay?

08:32.126 --> 08:34.788
Short haircut, stubby legs,
doesn't respond to my advances.

08:34.896 --> 08:36.864
You haven't answered my question!

08:36.964 --> 08:40.264
- Why the hell does Stewie look like this?
- Well, I took him to the gym,

08:40.369 --> 08:42.667
and the colorful gent there advised me
that I put him on steroids.

08:42.771 --> 08:43.739
And you listened to him?

08:43.840 --> 08:44.807
Yeah. I believe everything
everyone tells me anywhere.

08:48.948 --> 08:50.382
What's going on, B minus?

08:51.885 --> 08:53.944
- What's the haps?
- Stewie, you look gross.

08:54.054 --> 08:55.715
You look like Lou Ferrigno's poop.

08:55.822 --> 08:57.688
I look like a guy
who's been hitting the gym.

08:57.792 --> 08:59.726
It has nothing to do with the gym.
You're on drugs.

08:59.827 --> 09:02.625
Doesn't matter how you find
the pot of gold, B to the Ryan.

09:02.730 --> 09:04.858
All that matters
is that you beat the leprechauns.

09:04.967 --> 09:05.991
That doesn't make any sense.

09:06.101 --> 09:07.728
It doesn't have to make sense
when you look like this!

09:08.937 --> 09:11.839
I am hotter than phone sex
with a blind girl.

09:12.275 --> 09:15.642
- You sound hot. What are you wearing?
- I don't know.

09:24.489 --> 09:28.448
<i>Classic rock 103.7, WHGT.</i>

09:28.560 --> 09:29.755
I hate this station.

09:29.862 --> 09:32.228
They always make promises
they can't deliver.

09:32.331 --> 09:35.768
<i>Playing the greatest
rock-and-roll hits of all time!</i>

09:37.638 --> 09:39.367
- See?
- Chris, turn that off.

09:39.473 --> 09:41.498
We have a lot of work to do
before we go inside.

09:42.677 --> 09:45.578
All right. If I'm gonna be seen with you,
we have to do something about that look.

09:45.680 --> 09:47.307
Now, take that hat off.

09:48.951 --> 09:52.648
Oh, God! Your hair's all combed.
Here. Let me fix that.

09:53.522 --> 09:58.085
All right, good. Now let's give you
a pencil-thin douchebag beard.

09:58.395 --> 10:00.363
Oh, heavens! I look like a rake.

10:00.464 --> 10:02.831
No, you look like you don't care,
and that's good.

10:02.934 --> 10:04.060
Oh. Okay.

10:04.168 --> 10:08.071
Um, if we're dating, does that mean
when we go in there I can hold your hand?

10:08.173 --> 10:10.971
Good idea.
Then everyone will think you're popular.

10:11.076 --> 10:12.634
Well, I don't really care about that.

10:12.745 --> 10:15.647
I want to hold your hand 'cause I like you.

10:15.749 --> 10:16.875
I don't understand.

10:16.983 --> 10:19.884
Well, I think you're nice,
and I like spending time with you.

10:19.986 --> 10:24.048
You're really pretty, and I hope
I get to be with you for a long time.

10:24.158 --> 10:25.125
Wow.

10:25.226 --> 10:26.215
Um...

10:26.327 --> 10:28.990
No guy has ever said anything
that nice to me before.

10:29.097 --> 10:31.725
Well, maybe you've been hanging
around with jerks.

10:31.833 --> 10:34.234
Yeah, maybe I have.

10:34.871 --> 10:37.635
Hey, forget the pep rally.
You want to go see a movie?

10:37.740 --> 10:39.469
Cool. Maybe we could go see

10:39.575 --> 10:43.137
<i>that Chazz Palminteri/Paul Sorvino movie,
Distracting Trumpet.</i>

10:43.413 --> 10:45.643
I want to thank you all
for coming out here today.

10:45.749 --> 10:47.684
We got a serious situation
down in the Bronx.

10:48.887 --> 10:51.685
Our friend needs to get a message
to the short man in the hat.

10:52.892 --> 10:54.382
He needs to deliver this message

10:54.493 --> 10:57.326
before the construction-site contracts
are handed down.

10:58.531 --> 11:02.798
It's of vital importance
that these matters be attended to!

11:02.903 --> 11:06.237
So we may have to bring in our friend
from Yonkers!

11:06.340 --> 11:07.432
What?

11:07.542 --> 11:11.410
I said we may have to bring in our friend
from Yonkers!

11:16.652 --> 11:18.313
- Hey, what the hell?
- What, what, what?

11:18.420 --> 11:20.013
Is there a problem? Huh? You want to go?

11:20.123 --> 11:22.182
- You want to go?
- Go? What are you talking about?

11:22.292 --> 11:24.556
I'm talking about go.
That's what I'm talking about!

11:24.661 --> 11:26.493
- First one's on the house!
- I got things to do.

11:26.597 --> 11:28.792
- Where do you think you're going?
- I'm going downstairs.

11:28.899 --> 11:31.333
- There's a toll in the hall now, 10 bucks.
- Look, can I...

11:31.435 --> 11:32.425
Uh!

11:32.537 --> 11:33.970
- I just...
- Uh!

11:34.072 --> 11:35.403
- Stewie...
- Uh!

11:35.640 --> 11:36.868
- Look...
- Uh!

11:37.008 --> 11:37.997
- Come on...
- Uh!

11:38.611 --> 11:39.839
- I...
- Uh!

11:39.946 --> 11:41.038
- Just...
- Uh!

11:41.147 --> 11:42.512
- You...
- Uh!

11:42.615 --> 11:43.843
- This is...
- Uh!

11:43.950 --> 11:44.940
- Can I...
- Uh!

11:45.185 --> 11:48.245
Ah! I was just messing with you, man!
You can do whatever you want.

11:48.355 --> 11:51.291
I was just kidding you.
Why are you so serious?

11:54.295 --> 11:57.321
All right, Chrissy. Here we go.

11:59.101 --> 12:00.363
Look!
Oh, my God!

12:00.469 --> 12:01.959
Is that Chris Griffin
with Connie D'Amico?

12:02.104 --> 12:03.093
I think it is!

12:03.205 --> 12:05.140
Wow! That makes him popular.

12:05.242 --> 12:07.267
Hey, Griffin!
Griff-a!

12:07.377 --> 12:08.366
Griff-amano!

12:12.208 --> 12:14.802
Wow! The jocks have never said hello
to me before.

12:14.911 --> 12:17.676
- Hi, you guys.
- Hey, Chris, after school today,

12:17.781 --> 12:18.907
we're gonna go to the pizza place

12:19.016 --> 12:21.541
and make that single mother
who works there feel like a slut.

12:21.652 --> 12:25.384
She's really sweet and struggling
to raise a family. It's gonna be great!

12:25.557 --> 12:28.685
Wow! You did it, Connie.
Chris Griffin is popular!

12:28.793 --> 12:31.695
- So are you gonna dump him now?
- No, Gina. I'm not.

12:31.797 --> 12:34.061
- You're not?
- No. There's something about him.

12:34.166 --> 12:37.466
He's not like the other guys.
I actually really like him.

12:37.571 --> 12:38.970
- You do?
- Yeah.

12:39.072 --> 12:42.975
In fact, I'm going to his house for dinner
tonight so I can meet his parents.

12:46.047 --> 12:49.677
Wow! Connie D'Amico
is coming to my house for dinner!

12:49.785 --> 12:51.685
I just hope Dad doesn't embarrass us

12:51.787 --> 12:54.119
like he did when that one-legged guy
came over.

12:54.623 --> 12:58.924
All right. Well, if you like movie trivia,
I got one that'll stump you. Ahh...

12:59.128 --> 13:02.724
Of course you're probably not really
into tibia... Trivia! Ahh...

13:03.367 --> 13:05.062
Boy! That global warming, huh?

13:05.169 --> 13:08.138
They say we lost a foot of snow
last winter... Ahh...

13:08.974 --> 13:13.172
Hey, how about another beer?
I bet you like the taste of hops... Ahh...

13:13.612 --> 13:15.478
You only have one leg, sir.

13:19.783 --> 13:22.218
Connie, it's so nice to meet you.

13:22.320 --> 13:25.687
We're so excited that Chris is finally
bringing a girl home for dinner.

13:25.790 --> 13:27.985
It's really nice to meet you too,
Mrs. Griffin.

13:28.093 --> 13:31.086
Um, do you mind if I ask
what's up with your baby?

13:31.197 --> 13:34.428
- I'm gonna go work out.
- Again? That's, like, the eighth time today.

13:34.533 --> 13:37.992
I'm not satisfied until every vein
is forced up against my skin.

13:38.105 --> 13:40.164
Look how vascular I am, Brian.

13:40.274 --> 13:43.369
If there's one thing women love,
it's a vascular man.

13:43.745 --> 13:47.044
<i>I've got veins</i>

13:47.683 --> 13:51.084
<i>They carry blood all over my body</i>

13:51.186 --> 13:53.677
That's how John Mayer would say it,
"body. "

13:53.789 --> 13:56.384
I'm really into him now.
You better be okay with it!

13:56.493 --> 14:00.190
Well, to answer your question, Connie,
apparently, I'm married to a man

14:00.297 --> 14:03.358
who thinks it's okay
to inject an infant with steroids.

14:03.467 --> 14:06.595
Wait, Lois. Knock it off for a sec.
Connie, you are really pretty.

14:06.704 --> 14:09.139
I mean, you have filled out
something whacky.

14:09.241 --> 14:11.300
Oh! Thanks, Mr. Griffin.

14:11.410 --> 14:13.743
- I like what you're doing with your boobs.
- Dad!

14:13.846 --> 14:16.007
So, Connie,
now that you're dating my brother,

14:16.115 --> 14:17.582
maybe we can hang out, you know?

14:17.684 --> 14:20.017
Hey! After dinner,
you want to come up to my room

14:20.120 --> 14:23.385
- and give each other makeovers?
- I don't use makeup, Meg.

14:23.490 --> 14:25.515
Of course you don't. You're all natural.

14:25.626 --> 14:27.356
Man, your dad must be proud!

14:27.462 --> 14:30.431
Actually, my dad passed away
four years ago.

14:30.532 --> 14:35.493
Yeah, yeah, he did. He sure did.
You gonna shower before dessert?

14:38.341 --> 14:40.333
Greggy! Fitzy!

14:40.444 --> 14:42.674
T- Bone! Gaggaboo!

14:42.779 --> 14:45.612
- Nazi guy!
- Griff-a!

14:45.716 --> 14:48.618
Hey, we're totally stoked
for your party this weekend!

14:48.720 --> 14:51.780
You know it, brother.
It's gonna be awesome.

14:51.889 --> 14:55.291
But keep it on the down low
so the spazoids don't catch wind.

14:56.495 --> 14:59.488
- Speaking of spazoids.
- Wow!

14:59.599 --> 15:00.725
Can you believe it, Connie?

15:00.834 --> 15:03.496
You and I are going to be
at the same party this weekend!

15:03.603 --> 15:05.036
This is so cool!

15:05.138 --> 15:08.040
Hey, what are you wearing, so I make sure
I don't wear the same thing?

15:08.142 --> 15:10.838
- Um, you're not invited, Meg.
- What?

15:11.278 --> 15:14.840
- But it's at my house.
- Uh, Connie, let me handle this.

15:14.950 --> 15:16.679
I'm sorry, Meg. You can't come.

15:16.785 --> 15:20.051
There's an ass-to-boob ratio
that you're way off of.

15:21.157 --> 15:22.146
Hey, Chris, come on!

15:22.258 --> 15:25.786
Let's corner the nerds and call them gay
and make them show us their penises!

15:25.896 --> 15:28.296
- Won't that be gay of them?
- Yeah!

15:28.399 --> 15:29.593
That is grotacular!

15:29.700 --> 15:31.999
Way to go, man.
Awesome, bro.

15:43.803 --> 15:46.830
Man! Our boy Chris
partying with the cool kids.

15:46.941 --> 15:50.776
I am a very proud dad right now.
And look at that Connie.

15:50.879 --> 15:52.540
Jesus Christ! I bet that thing's so tight
you've gotta call the city to get in there.

15:59.620 --> 16:03.488
Meg, sweetheart, why don't you
just go downstairs and join the party?

16:03.592 --> 16:05.059
I wasn't invited!

16:05.627 --> 16:08.095
I hate Chris! He's such a jerk!

16:08.196 --> 16:11.826
Oh, look, honey. He's just a little confused
about who he is right now.

16:11.934 --> 16:14.960
I'm sure deep down
he still loves his big sister.

16:15.071 --> 16:19.566
I hate my school! I hate everyone!
I hate my life!

16:19.743 --> 16:22.234
Okay, look, Meg.
I've been at this for 45 minutes.

16:22.346 --> 16:24.042
I don't know what else I can say.

16:24.149 --> 16:26.344
Here's a Sylvia Plath book
and a bottle of Ambien.

16:26.451 --> 16:29.215
I'm gonna look the other way,
and whatever happens happens.

16:29.387 --> 16:31.117
<i>Party music</i>

16:31.223 --> 16:32.690
<i>Party song</i>

16:32.791 --> 16:34.520
<i>Does not attract attention</i>

16:34.627 --> 16:36.926
<i>Suggests a good time</i>

16:37.030 --> 16:39.726
- Gina, have you seen Chris?
- Yeah. He's over there.

16:43.471 --> 16:45.029
Chris! What are you doing?

16:45.139 --> 16:48.472
- Getting scraped to death by my zipper.
- You bastard!

16:48.609 --> 16:52.603
How the hell can you be cheating on me?
I'm the one who made you popular!

16:52.714 --> 16:55.980
No, Connie. Beating up
that Jewish kid made me popular.

16:56.085 --> 16:59.111
Come on, girls!
Let's go upstairs and make out!

17:01.257 --> 17:02.850
Oh, no! Connie's been hurt!

17:02.960 --> 17:06.293
I guess I should lie on top of her
to keep her warm.

17:07.531 --> 17:09.500
What are you looking at? It's a cartoon!

17:13.538 --> 17:16.064
Chris, I can't believe
you dissed Connie at your party.

17:16.175 --> 17:17.335
- That was awesome!
- Yeah.

17:17.443 --> 17:20.241
I heard about it when I was
making that gay nerd spoon with me.

17:20.346 --> 17:23.145
- Hey, guys. Room for one more?
- I don't think so.

17:23.250 --> 17:24.239
Loser.

17:24.351 --> 17:25.318
Reject!

17:25.419 --> 17:26.545
Everyone's gay but me.

17:30.964 --> 17:33.194
My God! He's practically ruined me.

17:33.300 --> 17:36.634
I've created a monster.
Meg, we've got to do something.

17:36.738 --> 17:38.433
We? Are you kidding?

17:38.606 --> 17:40.905
Do you really think
I would help you out in any way

17:41.010 --> 17:44.173
- after everything you've done to me?
- What are you talking about?

17:44.280 --> 17:45.406
You see this, Connie?

17:45.514 --> 17:48.609
This is from when you called me
"sticky-ass cow" in sixth grade.

17:48.718 --> 17:52.620
This one is from when you made
a plaster cast of my vagina freshman year.

17:52.722 --> 17:54.452
You want my help?
You can go fuck yourself!

17:55.660 --> 17:57.560
Hey, Meg! Think fast!
Ah!

17:57.662 --> 18:01.099
Loser!
- All right, let's do it.

18:01.200 --> 18:03.100
When we're done with him,
he'll be more of an outcast

18:03.202 --> 18:05.136
than a seagull at an Adam Sandler movie.

18:08.708 --> 18:12.474
<i>This is my old bicycle that I had
from when I was 10.</i>

18:14.448 --> 18:17.975
<i>Sometimes the banana seat
hurts my heinie.</i>

18:19.688 --> 18:22.156
- Will you shut up?
- You shut up, man! It's a comedy!

18:22.257 --> 18:25.658
<i>When I ring the bell,
it makes my pants feel funny.</i>

18:25.761 --> 18:27.195
<i>Ring, ring, ring.</i>

18:34.271 --> 18:38.834
Ah! Another day of being huge.
Good morning, guns of...

18:38.944 --> 18:42.812
Oh, no! What's happening?

18:43.648 --> 18:46.243
I'll tell you what's happening.
Your steroids have worn off.

18:46.352 --> 18:47.819
You're weak like everyone else.

18:47.920 --> 18:50.582
And guess what?
There's a toll in the hall now.

18:50.690 --> 18:53.717
- Stay away from me! Stay away from me!
- Stewie, no!

19:00.568 --> 19:03.662
And now
here's something we hope you'll really like.

19:08.143 --> 19:11.739
<i>Settle down, everyone.
Okay. Let's get this assembly started.</i>

19:11.848 --> 19:13.076
Is everything set, Meg?

19:13.183 --> 19:15.708
Once Chris gets up there,
my friend in the A/V Department

19:15.819 --> 19:18.653
- will take care of everything.
- Okay, Meg. Remember our deal.

19:18.756 --> 19:21.554
I do this for you,
and I have your permission

19:21.659 --> 19:24.185
to think about you later tonight
when I'm in the tub.

19:24.296 --> 19:25.854
- Fine, Neil.
- Awesome!

19:25.964 --> 19:30.264
I might even go leftie tonight,
stranger in the tub.

19:30.569 --> 19:34.768
<i>Before we begin, Chris Griffin
has an announcement for the cool kids.</i>

19:34.974 --> 19:36.100
<i>Yeah, hey, guys.</i>

19:36.209 --> 19:39.145
<i>The meeting of the Cool Kids Club
will be at 3:15,</i>

19:39.246 --> 19:41.908
<i>leaning up against Tim Breckner's SUV
in the parking lot.</i>

19:53.154 --> 19:54.917
<i>Would you fuck me?</i>

19:56.390 --> 19:57.824
<i>I'd fuck me</i>

19:59.094 --> 20:00.721
<i>I'd fuck me so hard</i>

20:14.311 --> 20:16.473
<i>Hey, Chris. What's that?
Did you sit on something?</i>

20:22.346 --> 20:24.611
- Chris Griffin's a freak!
- What a loser!

20:24.716 --> 20:25.944
I'm gay, all right?

20:26.051 --> 20:29.112
Oh! Come on. It's me, Griff-a!

20:29.222 --> 20:30.951
You don't get to talk like that anymore!

20:31.457 --> 20:34.949
Connie, the person who humiliated you
has himself been humiliated.

20:35.061 --> 20:38.498
By the rules of high school,
you are now popular again.

20:38.832 --> 20:41.596
- Well, we did it, Connie.
- Thanks for your help, Meg.

20:41.702 --> 20:44.171
There's no chance
we're gonna be friends now, is there?

20:44.272 --> 20:45.500
Absolutely not.

20:45.607 --> 20:48.132
Can I at least think about you
in the tub later?

20:48.243 --> 20:51.077
- No!
- I'm still gonna.

20:54.650 --> 20:58.143
- Well, Chris, you must feel ridiculous.
- I do, Dad.

20:58.255 --> 21:00.849
And, Meg, I'm really sorry
I was such a douche.

21:00.957 --> 21:02.983
Well, there is a way
you can make it up to me.

21:03.094 --> 21:05.289
- How?
- Tell me what it was like

21:05.396 --> 21:06.556
being one of them.

21:06.664 --> 21:10.465
It was like basking in the warm glow
of a higher intelligence

21:10.569 --> 21:15.507
as it envelops you and allows you
to become part of its everlasting glory.

21:17.377 --> 21:18.503
I flew today.

21:18.504 --> 22:19.504
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru